tool.help:
NCBI EGAPx prepare input ========================
What it does ============
Downloads the data that an `EGAPx <https://github.com/ncbi/egapx>`_ run needs (EGAPx ``--download-needed``) into an **EGAPx local cache** dataset. It does not run the annotation. The cache holds the EGAPx support data and taxonomy database, the BUSCO lineage for the taxid (from busco-data.ezlab.org), every remote URL input (genome, reads, proteins), the SRA reads for runs or queries in the configuration, and any history or built-in datasets selected in the tool form. The compute node running this job needs Internet access.
Then run **NCBI EGAPx execute** with:
- the generated **EGAPx configuration** YAML (when configured via the tool form) or your history YAML configuration, and - this **EGAPx local cache** dataset.
To download and annotate in one step, use **NCBI EGAPx**.
